      "campaign_notes": [
        "Campaign of 2026-11-21 stopped early. Runs 1 to 4 of that session succeeded. Runs 5 to 9 returned HTTP 500 after 18.5s and then about 3s each, because the Anthropic API credit balance was exhausted mid campaign: 'Your credit balance is too low to access the Anthropic API' as a 400 invalid_request_error, retried 3 times by app.core.llm and surfaced as LLMCallError, which the route maps to 500. These are environment failures and not pipeline failures, so they are recorded as errors and excluded from the percentiles rather than counted as overruns. OpenAI backed calls, the critic and the embeddings, were unaffected. Five more successful runs are needed to close the Step 3.6 gate once the balance is topped up.",
        "Campaign completed 2026-11-22 after the Anthropic balance was topped up. All 5 remaining runs succeeded, so 10 successful runs are recorded and the Step 3.6 gate is MET. DEV observations only (R1): one machine, one brief, the emulator suite, live provider latency."
      ],
      "observations": {
        "latency_is_bimodal_on_the_critic_loop": "The 10 successful runs split into two non overlapping groups with nothing in between. Seven runs used 0 regeneration cycles and took 175.2 to 212.2s. Three runs used 2 cycles and took 422.9 to 470.6s. The gap between the slowest 0 cycle run and the fastest 2 cycle run is 210.7s, wider than the entire spread of either group. So the variance in NFR2b is not a spread at all, it is whether the FR3 self correction loop fired, and 2 cycles cost roughly 2.35 times a clean pass. The p95 of 470.6s is therefore a measure of the critic loop rather than of the pipeline, which is worth saying outright when defending the D13 re-scope: the worst observed run still finished inside 53 percent of the 900s budget.",
        "first_pass_critic_rejection_rate": "3 of 10 runs needed revisions. Of those, one ended approved after 2 cycles and two ended NOT approved, having reached the cycle cap. So 2 of 10 packages were delivered to the teacher without critic approval. That is not a defect, it is the reason the Review Dashboard shows the verdict and the open issues (FR5, Fig 7): a fifth of generated units arrive needing human judgement before they can be published.",
        "rouge_l_is_not_a_result": "Inline ROUGE-L ranged 0.1894 to 0.2483 across the 10 runs, measured against unit_01_math_fractions_g5, which is itself still a DRAFT and not teacher validated. Under R1 and D17 these are per draft diagnostics and cannot be read as an FR4 similarity result.",
        "r6_held_on_every_run": "All 10 runs passed the persistence check, including student_readable_docs_without_answers, so no answer field reached a student readable exercise doc in any run."
      }
    }
